# Decomp Tree V2 — Standard Workflow

When working on the decomp_tree_v2 extension, follow this workflow.

## 1. Plan first

- Think through the problem and read the codebase for relevant files.
- Write a plan to `projectplan.md` (in project root or decomp_tree_v2 as appropriate).
- The plan must include a list of todo items you can check off as you complete them.

## 2. Verify before coding

- Before starting implementation, check in with the user so they can verify the plan.

## 3. Execute and track

- Work through the todo items, marking each complete as you go.
- At every step, give a high-level explanation of what you changed.

## 4. Keep changes simple

- Make every task and code change as simple as possible.
- Avoid massive or complex changes.
- Each change should impact as little code as possible. Everything is about simplicity.

## 5. Review

- Add a review section to `projectplan.md` with a summary of the changes and any other relevant information.
